WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:13.933
Bottom line: pilot Copilot Code for one small purpose-built solution, with IT policy set first, a named owner, scoped data, a spend limit and an explicit stop-or-expand review.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:19.733
Code is for outcome-led builders, not a replacement for developer tools.

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:34.567
Describe a dashboard, team tool, site, transform, automation or script; Code builds a live preview, keeps revertible versions and can publish cloud apps to Copilot Managed Runtime for your organization.

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:46.700
Local mode works inside a chosen folder and asks approval by default for network, extensions or MCP, shell commands and outside-folder access.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.567
Cloud mode is isolated.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:58.167
Microsoft says existing Microsoft 365 governance applies, with audit visibility into code, commands and file activity.

00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:08.367
IT must confirm license and enablement, then set auto-approve, execution location, GitHub, organizational data and spend policies.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:18.867
Recommendation: one low-risk business use case, one owner, least data needed, a budget cap, and a stop-or-expand review before broader access.
